content.thinking:
Actually, this is cleaner. Hugo's Go template has the issue where declaring a variable with `:=` inside a block scopes it to that block, so the inside-if-else approach is safer. But there's actually no issue here. Let me make it even cleaner with a single block.

Actually let me think about this more carefully. In Hugo's Go template, `:=` declares within the current block scope. So if I do:

```
{{- if $isEn -}}
  {{- $headline := "Daily Spark" -}}
  ...
{{- else -}}
  {{- $headline := "今日小火花" -}}
  ...
{{- end -}}
```

The `$headline` variable doesn't leak outside the block. That's why I duplicated the markup. This works but is verbose. Let me use a cleaner approach: assign once based on the lang.

Actually a much simpler approach is to use `index` with a lookup map. Let me rewrite cleanly:

arguments.content:
{{- /*
  Renders the "Daily Spark" card on the home page.
  Reads site.Data.daily_spark (written by .github/workflows/daily-spark.yml).
  If the data file is missing or empty, nothing is rendered.
  Language-aware: switches headline / tag / title / task via .Lang.
*/ -}}

{{- $spark := site.Data.daily_spark -}}
{{- if and $spark (isset $spark "date") (isset $spark "zh") (isset $spark "en") -}}
  {{- $langKey := "zh" -}}
  {{- if eq .Lang "en" -}}
    {{- $langKey = "en" -}}
  {{- end -}}
  {{- $headline := "今日小火花" -}}
  {{- if eq $langKey "en" -}}
    {{- $headline = "Daily Spark" -}}
  {{- end -}}
  {{- $tag := index $spark.tag $langKey -}}
  {{- $title := index (index $spark $langKey) "title" -}}
  {{- $task := index (index $spark $langKey) "task" -}}

  <section class="daily-spark" aria-label="{{ $headline }}">
    <header class="daily-spark__head">
      <span class="daily-spark__label">{{ $headline }}</span>
      <time class="daily-spark__date" datetime="{{ $spark.date }}">{{ $spark.date }}</time>
    </header>
    <div class="daily-spark__body">
      <span class="daily-spark__tag">{{ $tag }}</span>
      <h2 class="daily-spark__title">{{ $title }}</h2>
      <p class="daily-spark__task">{{ $task }}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
{{- end -}}

{{- with site.Params.homeInfoParams }}
<article class="first-entry home-info">
    <header class="entry-header">
        <h1>{{ .Title | markdownify }}</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="entry-content md-content">
        {{ $opts := dict "display" "block" }}
        {{ .Content | $.Page.RenderString $opts }}
    </div>
    <footer class="entry-footer">
        {{ partial "social_icons.html" (dict "align" site.Params.homeInfoParams.AlignSocialIconsTo) }}
    </footer>
</article>
{{- partial "daily_spark.html" . -}}
{{- end -}}

